<title>RUSSIA: Russian government taxes most white sugar imports.</title>
<headline>Russian government taxes most white sugar imports.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia will levy a 25 percent duty on all white sugar imports from May 15, but the tariff will not apply to Belarus, Kazakhstan and Kyrgyzstan, which have a customs treaty with Russia, a government decree said.</p>
<p>A copy of the decree, dated April 11 and received by Reuters on Tuesday, said the 25 percent tariff would be no lower than 0.07 European currency units, or Ecus, per kg.</p>
</text>
